md`## Notebook Kit cells

- \`cellLanguage\` routes a cell to [js-toolchain](https://observablehq.com/@tomlarkworthy/js-toolchain) when a variable has a Notebook Kit display state from a plain JavaScript definition, or its \`lang\` is exactly \`["js"]\`. A new cell follows its module: js if any existing cell is.
- \`sourceLanguage\` keeps a module with no Notebook Kit cell classic. Source only Notebook Kit parses (\`const x = 1;\`) goes to observablejs-toolchain there and reports its syntax error.
- js cells compile with \`transpileJavaScript\` and apply through \`defineCell\`, which installs the \`display\` and \`view\` shadows. They edit in CodeMirror's JavaScript language; the linter reports that language's syntax-tree errors.
- A Notebook Kit \`viewof x = …\` or \`mutable x = …\` cell routes to observablejs-toolchain: js-toolchain has no ojs dialect.`
